ility varied significantly across different market sentiment conditions.\n\nThe highest average Closed PnL was observed during Greed sentiment, indicating that traders performed better in bullish market conditions with stronger market confidence and momentum.\n\nFear sentiment also showed positive average profitability, suggesting that some traders were able to capitalize on market volatility during uncertain periods.\n\nNeutral market conditions produced the lowest average profit, indicating relatively weaker trading opportunities and lower market momentum.\n\nOverall, the results suggest that market sentiment plays an important role in influencing trader performance and profitability.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 2. Trading Volume by Market Sentiment","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Convert Size USD to numeric\n\ntrader_df['Size USD'] = pd.to_numeric(\n    trader_df['Size USD'],\n    errors='coerce'\n)\n\n# Trading volume by sentiment\n\nvolume_analysis = merged_df.groupby(\n    'classification'\n)['Size USD'].sum()\n\nprint(volume_analysis)\n\n# Plot\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n\nplt.bar(\n    volume_analysis.index,\n    volume_analysis.values\n)\n\nplt.title('Trading Volume by Market Sentiment')\n\nplt.xlabel('Sentiment')\n\nplt.ylabel('Total Trading Volume')\n\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\n\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-08T15:31:50.101314Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-08T15:31:50.102437Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-08T15:31:50.274853Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-08T15:31:50.102340Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-08T15:31:50.273820Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"classification\nExtreme Greed    3.940677e+07\nFear             7.041585e+08\nGreed            1.155037e+08\nNeutral          2.184323e+07\nName: Size USD, dtype: float64\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Insight\n\nThe trading volume analysis shows that the highest trading activity occurred during Fear market conditions.\n\nThis suggests that traders were highly active during uncertain or volatile market phases, possibly attempting to manage risk, capture short-term opportunities, or react to sudden market movements.\n\nGreed sentiment also showed strong trading participation, indicating increased confidence and bullish market behavior.\n\nIn contrast, Neutral market conditions recorded the lowest trading volume, reflecting lower market excitement and reduced trading activity.\n\nOverall, the results indicate that both fear-driven volatility and bullish market sentiment significantly influence trader participation in the market.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 3. Trading Volume by Market Sentiment","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"side_analysis = merged_df.groupby(\n    ['classification', 'Side']\n).size().unstack()\n\nprint(side_analysis)\n\nside_analysis.plot(\n    kind='bar',\n    figsize=(10,6)\n)\n\nplt.title('Buy vs Sell Activity by Sentiment')\n\nplt.xlabel('Sentiment')\n\nplt.ylabel('Number of Trades')\n\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\n\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-08T15:32:08.101050Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-08T15:32:08.101959Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-08T15:32:08.456911Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-08T15:32:08.101920Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-08T15:32:08.455806Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Side              BUY   SELL\nclassification              \nExtreme Greed    3371   3591\nFear            66081  67790\nGreed           15421  20868\nNeutral          3505   3636\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Insight\n\nThe Buy vs Sell analysis reveals that SELL trades were slightly higher than BUY trades across all market sentiment categories.\n\nDuring Fear sentiment, trading activity was significantly higher compared to other market conditions, indicating increased market participation and possible panic-driven or defensive trading behavior.\n\nGreed sentiment also showed strong trading activity, with SELL positions noticeably exceeding BUY positions. This may suggest profit-booking behavior or increased short-term trading during bullish conditions.\n\nExtreme Greed and Neutral conditions showed comparatively lower trading activity, reflecting fewer market participants during those phases.\n\nOverall, the analysis highlights how market sentiment strongly influences trader behavior and trading decisions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 4. Trading Fee Analysis","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Convert Fee column\n\ntrader_df['Fee'] = pd.to_numeric(\n    trader_df['Fee'],\n    errors='coerce'\n)\n\nfee_analysis = merged_df.groupby(\n    'classification'\n)['Fee'].mean()\n\nprint(fee_analysis)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n\nplt.bar(\n    fee_analysis.index,\n    fee_analysis.values\n)\n\nplt.title('Average Trading Fee by Sentiment')\n\nplt.xlabel('Sentiment')\n\nplt.ylabel('Average Fee')\n\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\n\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-05-08T15:32:18.355841Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-05-08T15:32:18.356933Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-05-08T15:32:18.502658Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-05-08T15:32:18.356842Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-05-08T15:32:18.501659Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"classification\nExtreme Greed    0.978567\nFear             1.083267\nGreed            0.670562\nNeutral          1.224461\nName: Fee, dtype: float64\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Insight\n\nThe fee analysis shows noticeable differences in trading costs across various market sentiment conditions.\n\nNeutral market conditions recorded the highest average trading fees, which may indicate relatively larger position sizes or inefficient trading activity during uncertain market direction.\n\nFear sentiment also showed high average fees, suggesting increased trading activity and frequent position changes during volatile market conditions.\n\nGreed sentiment had comparatively lower average fees, indicating more stable or efficient trading behavior during bullish phases.\n\nOverall, the analysis suggests that market sentiment affects not only trader profitability but also trading intensity and transaction costs.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Final Conclusion\n\nThis project analyzed the relationship between Bitcoin market sentiment and trader performance using historical trading data and the Fear & Greed Index.\n\nThe analysis revealed that market sentiment significantly influences profitability, trading activity, and trader behavior.\n\nGreed market conditions showed the highest average profitability, while Fear periods generated the highest trading activity. SELL trades slightly dominated across most sentiment conditions, indicating defensive or profit-booking behavior among traders.\n\nOverall, the project demonstrates that sentiment analysis can provide valuable insights into market psychology and trading strategy development.","metadata":{}}]}
